{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2CH",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover he made an altar of brass, twenty cubits the length of it, and twenty cubits the breadth of it, and ten cubits the hight of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also he made a molten sea of ten cubits from brim to brim, round in compass, and five cubits the hight of it; and a line of thirty cubits encompassed it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And under it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the similitude of oxen, which encompassed it: ten in a cubit, encompassing the sea. Two rows of oxen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cast, when it was cast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking towards the north, and three looking towards the west, and three looking towards the south, and three looking towards the east: and the sea ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was set",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " above upon them, and all their hinder parts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " inward.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the thickness of it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a hand-breadth, and the brim of it like the work of the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it received and held three thousand baths.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He made also ten lavers, and put five on the right hand, and five on the left, to wash in them: such things as they offered for the burnt-offering they washed in them; but the sea ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the priests to wash in.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he made ten candlesticks of gold according to their form, and set ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the temple, five on the right hand, and five on the left.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He made also ten tables, and placed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the temple, five on the right side, and five on the left. And he made a hundred basins of gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Furthermore he made the court of the priests, and the great court, and doors for the court, and overlaid the doors of them with brass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he set the sea on the right side of the east end, over against the south.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Huram made the pots, and the shovels, and the basins. And Huram finished the work that he was to make for king Solomon for the house of God;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To wit",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the two pillars, and the pommels, and the capitals ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the top of the two pillars, and the two wreaths to cover the two pommels of the capitals which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on the top of the pillars;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And four hundred pomegranates on the two wreaths; two rows of pomegranates on each wreath, to cover the two pommels of the capitals which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upon the pillars.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He made also bases, and lavers he made upon the bases;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "One sea, and twelve oxen under it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The pots also, and the shovels, and the flesh-hooks, and all their instruments, did Huram his father make to king Solomon for the house of the LORD of bright brass.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the plain of Jordan did the king cast them, in the clay ground between Succoth and Zeredathah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus Solomon made all these vessels in great abundance: for the weight of the brass could not be ascertained.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Solomon made all the vessels that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the house of God, the golden altar also, and the tables on which the show-bread ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was set",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ";",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Moreover the candlesticks with their lamps, that they should burn after the manner before the oracle, of pure gold;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the flowers, and the lamps, and the tongs, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "made he of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that perfect gold;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CH.4.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CH.4.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the snuffers, and the basins, and the spoons, and the censers, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure gold: and the entry of the house, the inner doors of it for the most holy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and the doors of the house of the temple, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " gold.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
